{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "במקהלות", :translit "b'mikh'helot", :gloss "in assemblies"} {:he "ע\"ש ויקהלו על משה ועל אהרן", :translit "azkir shemo vayakhelu al moshe v'al aharon", :gloss "see above and they assembled against Moses and against Aaron"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Cross-reference to Numbers 16:3 (קרח ויקהלו על משה ועל אהרן) flagged by abbreviation ע\"ש."}], :frame {:text "The phrase ויקהלו על משה ועל אהרן appears in Numbers 16:3, where Korah's faction assembles against Moses and Aaron. Ba'al HaTurim links the place-name מקהלות in the wilderness station list to that gathering.", :sources ["Numbers 16:3"]}} {:quotes [{:he "במקהלות", :translit "b'mikh'helot", :gloss "in assemblies"} {:he "במקהלות ברכו אלהים", :translit "b'mikh'helot barchu elohim", :gloss "in assemblies bless God"} {:he "ויסעו מחרדה", :translit "vayis'u m'kharada", :gloss "and they journeyed from Haradah"} {:he "מחרדת מצרים", :translit "m'kharadat mitzrayim", :gloss "fear of Egypt"} {:he "ויחנו במקהלות", :translit "vayachanu b'mikh'helot", :gloss "and they encamped in Makhelot"} {:he "קהלות קהלות", :translit "k'halot k'halot", :gloss "assemblies assemblies"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["במקהלות" "במקהלות ברכו אלהים"]}], :frame {:text "The phrase ברכו אלהים במקהלות occurs in Psalms 68:27. The Talmud derives that even infants (and by extension fetuses) recited the Song at the Sea, as stated in Sotah 30b and expanded in parallel midrashic traditions (e.g., Tanchuma Beshalach). Ba'al HaTurim reads the station name מחרדה as 'fear of Egypt' pursuing Israel, and מקהלות as Israel forming assembly after assembly to sing the song at the Sea.", :sources ["Psalms 68:27" "Sotah 30b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Cross-reference to Numbers 16:3 (קרח ויקהלו על משה ועל אהרן) flagged by abbreviation ע\"ש.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["במקהלות" "במקהלות ברכו אלהים"], :by :selah, :located [{:phra